WIRE.md §5.3: a `@json(bits)` list holding the same member twice has no encoding, E8102 at the repeated member, checked in verification; a list of distinct members and the empty list are fine.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Flag.
enum Flag @codes(UInt32) { tradable = 1, droppable = 2, soulbound = 4 }

/// Box.
record Box {
  /// Flags.
  flags: [Flag] @json(bits)
}

/// Box.
let box: Box = { flags: [tradable, soulbound, tradable] }

/// Fine.
let fine: [Box] = [{ flags: [soulbound, tradable] }, { flags: [] }]
-- project.canon --
project demo {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E8102]  a/a.canon:14:47
  box.flags: [tradable, soulbound, tradable] has no wire form for flags: tradable appears twice in a bits set

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
